					<![CDATA[
						 <p>(yes, I know I'm answering a post that's over 18 months old. Don't care; it's funny.)</p> <p>I got nitpicky enough to want to see what the original version of Circeus's post was.</p> <p>Due to a typo, instead of saying "reassembling <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-529">Josie</a>", he originally said "reassing Josie".</p> <p>Except that "re-assing" her is exactly what would happen.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-136461#post-407944</guid>
				<title>Re:</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-136461/scp-568#post-407944</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Mar 2009 15:02:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Agent Circeus</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>276761</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Well, this assumes of course that Josie was taken apart with it. Several details (notably the fact her front half moves as if the back one was still attached, and she does not control the other half) indicates it is not the case. it's still an amusing prospect. Reassembling Josie could totally become a new running joke <em>à la</em> killing <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-682">682</a>.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
